   "note": "Level 2 tips the no-fault gait from about 24 degrees, level 1 from about 27 (both hold at 20). The level-2 controller keeps the commanded centre of pressure within 90% of the foot, a margin the level-1 limit (A3) does not have: with the full foot, level 2 holds 25 and tips at 26. The ankle stays below its torque limit (15.5 of 20 kN m at 25 degrees). Level 2 is the more pessimistic; the slope limit should rest on it."
